:HELP NAME=ADDSCHIDXE.Add Search Index Entry (ADDSCHIDXE)
:P.Use the Add Search Index Entry (ADDSCHIDXE) command to add a panel
group's help topics to a search index.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDSCHIDXE/SCHIDX'.Search index (SCHIDX)
:P.The search index for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDSCHIDXE/PNLGRP'.Panel group (PNLGRP)
:P.The panel group, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTMNU.Create Menu (CRTMNU)
:P.Use the Create Menu (CRTMNU) command to create a menu object over a
panel group, a display file or a program.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/MENU'.Menu (MENU)
:P.The menu for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/TYPE'.Menu type (TYPE)
:P.The menu type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UIM, *DSPF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/PNLGRP'.Panel group (PNLGRP)
:P.The panel group, by name and library.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MENU.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/DSPF'.Display file (DSPF)
:P.The display file for this command.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MENU.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MENU.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MENU.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/CMDLIN'.Command line (CMDLIN)
:P.The command line for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LONG, *SHORT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/CHKLIBL'.Check library list (CHKLIBL)
:P.The check library list for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCHK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/CURLIB'.Current library (CURLIB)
:P.The current library of the job&colon. the library searched first by
name (after the system part of the library list) and where *CURLIB puts
new objects.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOCHG:EPK.
:PD.Not changed.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MNULIB, *CRTDFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/PRDLIB'.Product library (PRDLIB)
:P.The product library of the command&colon. it is added to the library
list while the command runs.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOCHG:EPK.
:PD.Not changed.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/REPLACE'.Replace menu (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMNU/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTPNLGRP.Create Panel Group (CRTPNLGRP)
:P.Use the Create Panel Group (CRTPNLGRP) command to create a panel
group from UIM source.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/PNLGRP'.Panel group (PNLGRP)
:P.The panel group, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PNLGRP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/INCFILE'.Include file (INCFILE)
:P.The source file that /COPY and /INCLUDE directives without a file
name search.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCFILE:EPK.
:PD.The source file of the object.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/OPTION'.Source listing options (OPTION)
:P.The source listing options for this command.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SRC:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK.*SOURCE:EPK.
:PD.The source.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOSRC:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*NOSOURCE:EPK.
:PD.No source listing.
:PT.:PK.*LIST:EPK.
:PD.A list is shown.
:PT.:PK.*NOLIST:EPK.
:PD.No list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/CHRID'.Character identifier (CHRID)
:P.The graphic character set and code page of the data.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Graphic character set
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Code page
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/REPLACE'.Replace panel group (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTPNLGRP/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTSCHIDX.Create Search Index (CRTSCHIDX)
:P.Use the Create Search Index (CRTSCHIDX) command to create an empty
search index for help.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSCHIDX/SCHIDX'.Search index (SCHIDX)
:P.The search index for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSCHIDX/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSCHIDX/REPLACE'.Replace search index (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTMNU.Delete Menu (DLTMNU)
:P.Use the Delete Menu (DLTMNU) command to delete menus.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTMNU/MENU'.Menu (MENU)
:P.The menu for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTPNLGRP.Delete Panel Group (DLTPNLGRP)
:P.Use the Delete Panel Group (DLTPNLGRP) command to delete panel
groups.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTPNLGRP/PNLGRP'.Panel group (PNLGRP)
:P.The panel group, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
